2026-11-05T23:44:41.2411345Z             "body": "This draft implements the frontend portion of Phase 2: customer identity and database sessions, audience-specific service adapters, course authoring and learner routes, account lifecycle orchestration, and whole-operation writer admission with pending-SQL release coordination. It consumes PR #91 unchanged and reconciles PR #92 as a source predecessor, preserving its execution core and original evidence.\n\nThe reviewed contract bundle currently pins Course `2847d953` and Community `5709ab0a`; both API draft PRs have passing required CI. Independent review identified a Course OpenAPI admin-security declaration mismatch that is being corrected before final repinning. Existing runtime admin enforcement remains separate.\n\nValidation at frontend `f561025a`: 2,539 unit tests passed with no failures/skips. Type-checking passed; lint has no errors. Component evidence includes 43 actual identity entry-point cases and 33 identity/lifecycle database cases, 28 learner fixture plus four legacy browser scenarios, four actual-stack authoring scenarios, and actual three-repository lifecycle/TLS/workload fixtures. Source records distinguish intercepted providers from deployed evidence and preserve failures.\n\nThe approved lifecycle policy and paid-course archive policy are recorded. This draft remains incomplete while the provider/coordinator join, export-cleanup physical-receipt correction, actual Course-backed learner qualification and final frontend CI/native artifact qualification continue. Real staging Google/Resend/Mux and deployed customer/authoring/access/lifecycle certification, P2-12 and G2 remain open.\n\nNo staging migration, provider/credential change, scheduler activation, frontend promotion or production activation is authorized by this PR. Dardan must start the concrete reviewed staging release under the single-operator policy. Phase 3, paid checkout, new Community member features and monitoring remain outside scope.\n\nSee `API-INTEGRATION-EXECUTION.md`, `docs/api-integration/phase2-goal.md` and the exact evidence in `docs/api-integration/baselines/2026-11-05-p2-contract-and-api-milestone/`.",
